  "foaf:name": "Opportunity through organized Tristate Stewardship",
  "sdo:name": "Opportunity through organized Tristate Stewardship",
  "sdo:description": "Palau’s Ngaremeduu Conservation Area (NCA), a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve, boasts Micronesia’s most diverse ecosystems—forests, rivers, mangroves, seagrass, and reefs—supporting dugongs, hawksbill turtles, and saltwater crocodiles. As Palau’s largest watershed, it connects Ngeremlengui, Ngatpang, and Aimeliik, whose communities share deep cultural ties to its resources. The NCA faces pressures from sedimentation, overharvesting, invasive species, climate change, and development. The project strengthens governance and stewardship through five priorities: community capacity building, enhanced resilience via coordination, eco-tourism promotion and sustainable livelihoods, reduced land-based sediment and pollution, and awareness fostering through education. By aligning management and empowering communities, ROOTS-NCA safeguards biodiversity, food security, and cultural heritage, ensuring the NCA’s endurance for future generations and serving as a model for community-led island resilience.",
